-- title:
--   Breadth-first search program and shortest-path result contract
-- statement:
--   The concrete FIFO breadth-first search uses a read-only arrays-of-arrays graph, a distance sentinel of −1, a parent array, and an explicitly instrumented graph_work clock. The generated public Call relation fixes its operational meaning. Its postcondition requires a fresh result object and two distinct fresh arrays, shortest attained distances to exactly the reachable vertices, −1 at unreachable vertices, predecessor edges decreasing distance by one, and preservation of caller storage. A valid source is required by the open goals; there is no valid source in an empty graph. This bundle supplies the implementation and specification only.
-- source:
--   CLRS, Introduction to Algorithms, fourth edition (MIT Press, 2022), Chapter 20, §20.2. https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262046305/introduction-to-algorithms/ ; new arrays-of-arrays implementation compiled with Algo2Lean v0.1.4, https://www.algo2lean.com/versions/v0.1.4/ . Source filenames and full code are in the mission description.

